{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"CHECKED FOR SUPERSESSION BY eb58, and this ticket is NOT superseded — recording the check so the next agent does not re-open the question or, worse, skip the ticket as redundant.\n\nThe suspicion was reasonable: eb58 (Model classes: trivial/standard/frontier) just closed with all six children done, and THIS ticket's problem statement says \"there is no way to express [per-pass models] on any non-default provider\" — which sounds like exactly what eb58 delivered.\n\nThe distinction is MECHANISM vs CONSUMER:\n* eb58 delivered the mechanism — per-class slots (`[tool.rebar.llm.model_classes]`), the nine `REBAR_LLM_<CLASS>_<FIELD>` overrides, per-class fallback chains, class-aware resolution, and the REBAR_LLM_MODEL deprecation/fan-out.\n* THIS ticket makes the GATES actually USE it per pass. Verified against the shipped YAML: the code-review gate's `verify` step already declares `model: standard` (landed by 172e), but `base` (Pass-1) and `coach` (Pass-4) still inherit `cfg.model` implicitly. Nothing in eb58 changed those.\n* Its ACs also demand things eb58 does not assert: that the RESOLVED model per pass is the intended class under a BEDROCK configuration, and that no bare `claude-*` id resolves to provider `anthropic` during a run configured for another provider. Those are cross-provider resolution guarantees, not class-plumbing.\n\nSo eb58 is a PREREQUISITE that is now satisfied, which is why this ticket became ready. `rebar ready` lists it as unblocked.\n\nMETHOD NOTE while I am here: I initially read this ticket's `deps` field (and 8625's) as the blocker list and concluded 8625 had none. WRONG — `deps` was `[]` on 8625 while the plan-review precheck correctly refused it as \"blocked by unclosed ticket(s) eb58, eb6e\". Blocking comes from LINK relations, not that field. `rebar ready` is the authoritative claimability check. The gate fast-failed with NO LLM spend, so the misread cost nothing — that fast-fail is doing real work."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785596755498026001,"uuid":"5e75d6ac-1f41-45af-bd69-b2a34a0a63a9"}